    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **26 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**. BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` from `'<LAST3>-<NNNN>'` (global sequence) to `'<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>'` (per-city sequence).\n\n**Changes in `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. **`nextCustomerCode`** now takes the city as well as the last name, and:\n   - `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n   - `NNNN` = a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, one more than the number of owners already in that city (counted case-insensitively via the existing `normalizeForHousehold` helper, consistent with how the code already keys on names/addresses)\n2. Extracted a small `first3Upper` helper for the shared prefix logic.\n3. Updated the call site (`addOwner`) to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\n**Values derived from `customerCode` rebuild automatically:** the `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is computed as `getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + <YY>`, so it now carries the new city-prefixed code with no further change needed \u2014 confirmed by Cp14.\n\nVerified: Cp16 (`[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`), Cp09 (two owners in \"Sydney\" \u2192 `SYD-ALP-0001` / `SYD-BRA-0002`, consecutive per-city sequence), Cp14 (membership number over the new code), and all 26 tests pass.",
